From cac27ff6b1e4c0b11f8ae06b1c0afd7a7294813d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:27:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Photo tab on the Mac (owner-approved design,
 plans/design/photo/)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Presets: a Preset chip in the bar (a small menu with search and covers),
  never a whole row; a preset locks Framing, Lens and Light to From preset.
- The stage: empty until this session's run (never an old result); the 4
  photos with a strip under the photo, Photo n of 4, Keep highlighted, Redo,
  Upscale, Use in Shot (the still as a video's start frame) and Share.
- The panel: Inputs (Character, Outfit, Product, References) with clear
  empty slots, then the Rig for a still (Framing, Lens, Light, Look, Style).
- The bar: Preset, Photos 1-4, Size (the shapes the model makes, from the
  estimate; hidden on an older server), Auto · <model>, and Generate with the
  real price, or Generate · 4 photos greyed with the reason beside it.
- The prompt hint names no one.
- Review mode: mac_<a|b>_photo_<empty|filled|results>_<w>x<h>.png at
  1000x700, 1152x720 and 1440x900 with photo_fits, photo_price,
  photo_empty_stage, photo_carousel and photo_presets in
  suite-design-check.txt; photo_restart now expects an empty stage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Py2rxoXQmfbR7CXwb939GC
